      "url": "https://www.archdaily.com/1187840/gca-architects",
      "title": "GCA Architects",
      "content_html": "<p>This issue brings together, across 326 pages, forty years of work by the Barcelona-based studio GCA Architects, founded in 1986 by Josep Juanpere and Antonio Puig, through a selection of nineteen works —most from the past decade and a half— spanning its practice in corporate, hospitality and residential architecture. An architecture that integrates building and interior design within a single project, attentive to materiality and detail, and a trajectory that grew with the Barcelona that emerged from the Olympic years to become a benchmark practice.</p><p>Located mostly in Barcelona, the works span almost every typology and scale: from the corporate towers</p>",
